 (iv) pooled-gap control.  For each orientation [class n | class n+g] the 50 gaps g in 2..300 with both
      endpoints coprime to 6: [5|1] n=6k-1, g=2 mod 6 ; [1|5] n=6k+1, g=4 mod 6 ; [5|5] n=6k-1, g=0 mod 6 ;
      [1|1] n=6k+1, g=0 mod 6.  D_g = N_ij - N_ji over k<=K ; pred_g = (R_i C_j - R_j C_i)/K from the pair's
      own marginals.  Block analysis: K split into 100 blocks (size K/100); p_(g,b) = block product of
      marginals, D_(g,b) = block discrepancy, r_(g,b) = D_(g,b) - p_(g,b).  Reported per orientation:
      pooled mean/sd(ddof=1)/#D_g>0 of D_g, mean pred_g ; corr and slope of block means m_b=mean_g D_(g,b)
      against p_b=mean_g p_(g,b) ; mean off-diagonal inter-gap correlation of D_(g,b) and of r_(g,b) over
      blocks ; residual test: RES = sum_b mean_g r_(g,b), SE = sd_b(mean_g r_(g,b))*sqrt(#blocks), z=RES/SE ;
      per-gap residual sd = sd_g(D_g - sum_b p_(g,b)).  The K=10^6 blocks are the first 100 blocks of
      10^4 centers; the K=10^7 blocks are 100 blocks of 10^5 centers (merged from 1000 blocks of 10^4).
      consistency: the block counts at the four control gaps reproduce the section 4(i) matrices  [PASS]

